IMPORT prelude

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore) -- market misconduct (Part 12): false trading and market rigging (s 197),
-- false or misleading statements (s 199), continuous disclosure (s 203), insider trading (ss 214 to 231), and the
-- consequences: criminal penalty (ss 204, 221), civil penalty (ss 232, 233) and compensation to investors (s 234).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SFA2001.txt
-- (amendments to Act 25 of 2021 shown in force).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 36 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository, the most of any Act not yet encoded.
-- The deposit runs to about 1.8 million characters; this row takes Part 12 Divisions 1, 3 and 4 only. Not encoded:
-- licensing of markets, clearing houses and intermediaries, prospectuses (Part 13), collective investment schemes,
-- takeovers, benchmarks (Part 12 Division 2), the corporate and partnership civil liability provisions (Division 5),
-- and disgorgement.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Securities and Futures Act 2001 -- market conduct`

§§ `197 -- false trading`

-- s 197(1): a person must not do anything whose purpose, or ANY of whose purposes, is to create a false or misleading
-- appearance of active trading or of the market or price. (1A): nor anything that creates or is likely to create that
-- appearance, if they know it will or are RECKLESS whether it will. (3), (5): the purpose is PRESUMED where a trade involves
-- no change in beneficial ownership (a wash trade, including through an associate) or where matching buy and sell orders
-- are placed. (4): rebuttable by the defendant.
DECLARE TradingConduct HAS
    `a purpose was to create a false appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `created or was likely to create a false appearance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or was reckless as to that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a wash trade or matched orders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant proved no such purpose` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A TradingConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false-appearance purpose is established` IF
        `the conduct`'s `a purpose was to create a false appearance`
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `was a wash trade or matched orders` AND (NOT `the conduct`'s `the defendant proved no such purpose`))

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A TradingConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct contravenes section 197` IF
        `the false-appearance purpose is established` `the conduct`
    OR  (`the conduct`'s `created or was likely to create a false appearance` AND `the conduct`'s `knew or was reckless as to that effect`)

§§ `199 -- false or misleading statements`

-- s 199: a person must not make a statement or disseminate information that is false or misleading in a material
-- particular and likely to induce dealing or to affect the market price, if they "(d) [do] not care whether [it] is true or
-- false; or (e) [know] or OUGHT REASONABLY TO HAVE KNOWN" that it is false or misleading.
--
-- Negligence is enough: a director who ought reasonably to have known a market announcement was misleading contravenes s 199.
DECLARE Statement HAS
    `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to induce dealing or move the price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maker knew` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maker ought reasonably to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maker did not care whether it was true` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the statement` IS A Statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement contravenes section 199` IF
        `the statement`'s `false or misleading in a material particular`
    AND `the statement`'s `likely to induce dealing or move the price`
    AND (    `the statement`'s `the maker knew`
         OR  `the statement`'s `the maker ought reasonably to have known`
         OR  `the statement`'s `the maker did not care whether it was true`)

§§ `203 -- continuous disclosure`

-- s 203(1): a listed entity must not "intentionally, recklessly or NEGLIGENTLY" fail to notify the exchange of information
-- the listing rules require. (3): "a contravention ... is NOT AN OFFENCE unless the failure to notify is intentional or
-- reckless". A negligent failure is still a contravention of Part 12 -- open to a civil penalty under s 232 and to
-- compensation claims under s 234 -- but not a crime.
DECLARE Fault IS ONE OF
    `intentional`
    `reckless`
    `negligent`
    `no fault`

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure failure contravenes section 203` IF
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `no fault` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the fault` IS A Fault
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure failure is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the fault`
    WHEN `intentional` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reckless` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `214 to 231 -- insider trading`

-- s 218: a person CONNECTED to a corporation (an officer, a substantial shareholder, or someone with access through a
-- professional or business relationship -- (5)) who possesses information that is not generally available and would be
-- expected to have a material effect on price, and who "KNOWS OR OUGHT REASONABLY TO KNOW" both of those things, must not deal,
-- procure dealing, or tip. (4): once possession and non-availability are proved, the connected person's knowledge is
-- PRESUMED until the contrary is proved.
-- s 219: anyone else (the "insider") is caught only if they "KNOWS" -- actual knowledge; no "ought reasonably to know", and no
-- presumption.
-- s 220: no need to prove intention to use the information.
-- s 215: information is generally available if readily observable, or announced and a reasonable period for dissemination has
-- passed, or deduced from such information.
-- s 228: an individual may deal knowing only of their OWN intention to deal.
-- s 231: defence if the other party to the trade knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information ("parity").
--
-- A director who ought to have realised the news was price-sensitive is caught; a friend at dinner who ought to have realised
-- it, but did not, is not. The negligence standard and the presumption apply only to the connected person.
DECLARE InsiderCase HAS
    `the person is connected to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `possessed the information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was generally available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was price-sensitive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `actually knew it was inside information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ought reasonably to have known it was inside information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rebutted the presumption of knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information was only of their own intended dealing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the counterparty knew or ought to have known it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dealt or procured dealing` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the case` IS AN InsiderCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the knowledge element is met` IF
    IF `the case`'s `the person is connected to the company`
    THEN     `the case`'s `actually knew it was inside information`
         OR  `the case`'s `ought reasonably to have known it was inside information`
         OR  (NOT `the case`'s `rebutted the presumption of knowledge`)
    ELSE `the case`'s `actually knew it was inside information`

GIVEN `the case` IS AN InsiderCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is insider trading` IF
        `the case`'s `dealt or procured dealing`
    AND `the case`'s `possessed the information`
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `the information was generally available`)
    AND `the case`'s `the information was price-sensitive`
    AND `the knowledge element is met` `the case`
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `the information was only of their own intended dealing`)
    AND (NOT `the case`'s `the counterparty knew or ought to have known it`)

GIVEN `announced` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reasonable period for dissemination has passed` IS A BOOLEAN, `readily observable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is generally available` IF
    `readily observable` OR (`announced` AND `a reasonable period for dissemination has passed`)

§§ `204, 221, 232, 233 -- criminal and civil penalties`

-- ss 204(1), 221(1): an offence -- a fine up to $250,000, imprisonment up to 7 years, or both.
-- s 232(2): on a balance of probabilities, a civil penalty up to the GREATER of 3 times the profit gained or loss avoided, and
-- $2 million. (3): not less than $100,000 for a corporation, $50,000 for anyone else.
-- ss 204(2), 221(2): no prosecution after a civil penalty order or agreement. s 233(2): no civil penalty action after a
-- conviction or acquittal (unless the acquittal was on withdrawal of the charge). (1): 6 years from the contravention.
GIVEN `profit gained or loss avoided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum civil penalty` MEANS
    IF 3 TIMES `profit gained or loss avoided` GREATER THAN 2000000
    THEN 3 TIMES `profit gained or loss avoided`
    ELSE 2000000

GIVEN `is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `is a corporation` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

DECLARE Prior IS ONE OF
    `nothing`
    `a civil penalty order or agreement`
    `a conviction`
    `an acquittal on the merits`
    `an acquittal on withdrawal of the charge`

GIVEN `what came first` IS A Prior
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may follow` IF
    CONSIDER `what came first`
    WHEN `a civil penalty order or agreement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a conviction` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an acquittal on the merits` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `what came first` IS A Prior, `years since the contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a civil penalty action may be commenced` IF
        `years since the contravention` AT MOST 6
    AND CONSIDER `what came first`
        WHEN `nothing` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an acquittal on withdrawal of the charge` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `234 -- compensation to investors`

-- s 234(1): a contravening person who GAINED A PROFIT OR AVOIDED A LOSS is liable to anyone who dealt in the same products
-- CONTEMPORANEOUSLY and lost by the price difference. (2), (6): capped at the "maximum recoverable amount" -- the profit
-- gained or loss avoided, less compensation already ordered to other claimants.
-- (1A): a person who contravened s 199, 200 or 201 by a false statement or concealment is liable "whether or not [they] had
-- gained a profit or avoided a loss" to anyone who dealt IN RELIANCE on it and suffered loss. (2A)(b): the reliance loss,
-- with NO maximum-recoverable cap.
-- (4): 6 years from completion of the dealing.
--
-- An insider who made $10,000 owes contemporaneous traders $10,000 between them, however much they lost. A company that
-- negligently issued a false announcement and made nothing owes each investor who relied on it their whole loss.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `the contravention was a false statement or concealment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant relied on it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant dealt contemporaneously` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant's loss` IS A NUMBER
    `the contravener's profit or loss avoided` IS A NUMBER
    `already ordered to other claimants` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remaining recoverable amount` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `the contravener's profit or loss avoided` GREATER THAN `the claim`'s `already ordered to other claimants`
    THEN `the claim`'s `the contravener's profit or loss avoided` MINUS `the claim`'s `already ordered to other claimants`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation recoverable` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `the contravention was a false statement or concealment` AND `the claim`'s `the claimant relied on it`
    THEN `the claim`'s `the claimant's loss`
    ELSE IF `the claim`'s `the claimant dealt contemporaneously` AND `the claim`'s `the contravener's profit or loss avoided` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `the claimant's loss`) (`the remaining recoverable amount` `the claim`)
         ELSE 0
